Static object permissions and placement, 2026-09-19.
Fixed image evo-flight-lab:sealed, linux/arm64, network none:
GCC 14.2.0-19 and Clang 19.1.7.
For each compiler, -O0/-O2 and [-fno-pic -fno-pie]/[-fPIC]:
  CC -std=gnu11 OPT MODEL -c tests/fixtures/static-readonly-storage.c -o case.o
  nm --defined-only case.o
  CC case.o -no-pie -o case; ./case
Eight compilations and executions succeed, all executions exit 0.
Both warn that literal discards const; the default case only reads it.

Both compilers place scalar, zero, array and device in read-only R storage;
pointers is R without PIC and relocatable read-only data (nm D) with PIC.
object, pointee, mixed, literal and mutable_literal are D in both modes.
The const compound literal is r; the non-const compound literal is d.
The function-static const object is r at O0 and folded away at O2.
Explicit .data.explicit conflicts: GCC makes it writable (D), Clang does not
(R). Existing explicit-section placement is retained; this fix changes only
automatic placement, not the permission interpretation of user section names.
None of the write-through-const cases 1..7 is claimed as defined C execution
or run natively; those are interpreter E3014 instrumentation assertions.

RED: missing readonly metadata in emitted global @scalar; C-HIR case 1
permits the store. Two declared failing tests, zero build errors.
Original trigger: mm/page_alloc.o zone_names and migratetype_names, both D
versus R in the GCC reference on the original non-PIC kernel command.

GREEN subject, target/frontend/release/evocc SHA-256:
2214908df66602b0fcbf72291e98f6909abcd2e391211f7cb279da27b8da860c
Forty language-semantic tests pass, including both interpreter permission
checks, shared EvoIR/EvoMIR metadata round trips, exact native placement and
EvoMIR E3014 execution. The independent checker accepts unchanged permission
and refuses a removed readonly field even with a recomputed output digest.
Const TLS initialization/permission and the exhaustive text-field sentinel
tests pass separately.
Default/-O2 times static/PIC assembly, each built and executed using GCC-14
and Clang-19: 8/8 exits 0 with the expected object symbol kinds. Linking uses
-no-pie -Wl,-z,relro,-z,now. No undefined write-through-const case runs natively.

The PIC fixture, emitted with -Dmain=readonly_entry, additionally passes
4/4 shared-library executions (default/-O2, GCC-14/Clang-19 assembler/linker):
  CC -shared OPT-dso.s -Wl,-z,relro,-z,now -o /tmp/libreadonly.so
  CC tests/fixtures/static-readonly-driver.c -ldl -o /tmp/driver
  /tmp/driver /tmp/libreadonly.so
Each DSO has .data.rel.ro covered by GNU_RELRO and no TEXTREL dynamic tag.
The driver loads, resolves, runs and closes the DSO; all four exit 0.
These checks were repeated with the same frozen assembly on 2026-09-19.

